// map: transform each Trade → BigDecimal (N trades → N amounts)
Stream<BigDecimal> amounts = trades.stream()
    .map(Trade::getAmount);  // INTERMEDIATE: 5 trades → 5 BigDecimals

// reduce: combine all BigDecimals → one total (N amounts → 1 total)
BigDecimal total = trades.stream()
    .map(Trade::getAmount)                           // transform: Trade → BigDecimal
    .reduce(BigDecimal.ZERO, BigDecimal::add);       // aggregate: all → one sum

// reduce with identity: guaranteed result (empty stream → identity)
BigDecimal sum = Stream.<BigDecimal>empty()
    .reduce(BigDecimal.ZERO, BigDecimal::add);  // → BigDecimal.ZERO (identity)

// reduce without identity: returns Optional (empty stream → Optional.empty())
Optional<BigDecimal> max = trades.stream()
    .map(Trade::getAmount)
    .reduce(BigDecimal::max);  // → Optional<BigDecimal>
```

**Three forms of reduce:**

```java
// Form 1: reduce(BinaryOperator) → Optional<T>
Optional<BigDecimal> max = amounts.stream().reduce(BigDecimal::max);

// Form 2: reduce(identity, BinaryOperator) → T
BigDecimal sum = amounts.stream().reduce(BigDecimal.ZERO, BigDecimal::add);

// Form 3: reduce(identity, BiFunction, BinaryOperator) → U
// For parallel: accumulator + combiner
BigDecimal total = trades.parallelStream()
    .reduce(BigDecimal.ZERO,
        (subtotal, trade) -> subtotal.add(trade.getAmount()),  // accumulator
        BigDecimal::add);                                       // combiner (parallel merge)
